# `++` between two Ints -- the same mistake the other way round.
#
# The pairing in `typesystem.ALTERNATIVES` runs both ways, so an
# operator written where its look-alike belongs names that look-alike
# whichever of the two was written.
#
# This program is expected to FAIL type checking. Its `.ast.out` holds
# the error message, not a program's output.

count = 2
total = count ++ 3
